      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Ask a yes or no question about every picture in a folder and sort them by the answer, in one Run. Here: is there a person in it? The people go to one folder, the rest to another. Use it to clean a big folder: keep only the sharp ones, only the ones with a face, only the landscapes.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Portraits</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Ask your own question</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Change the question in the <b>formula</b>, in the gear of <b>AI Prompt Pixaroma</b>, and keep the end: <i>Answer with one word only: yes or no.</i></li><li>Questions that work: <i>Is the picture sharp and in focus?</i>, <i>Is there any text or a watermark in the picture?</i>, <i>Is this a photo of food?</i>, <i>Is the main subject looking at the camera?</i></li><li>To keep the NO pictures instead, simply swap the two Save nodes' folders, or type <b>no</b> in Text Match.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Good to know</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>The AI can be wrong on borderline pictures. Check the folders after a big Run.</li><li>Your original pictures are not moved: each one is saved as a copy into its folder.</li><li>Text Match works with any text, not only yes and no: it can look for several words and tells you which one it found.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-ai-prompt-local\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">What AI Prompt needs</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Ask a yes or no question about every picture in a folder and sort them by the answer, in one Run. Here: is there a person in it? The people go to one folder, the rest to another. Use it to clean a big folder: keep only the sharp ones, only the ones with a face, only the landscapes.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Portraits</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Ask your own question</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Change the question in the <b>formula</b>, in the gear of <b>AI Prompt Pixaroma</b>, and keep the end: <i>Answer with one word only: yes or no.</i></li><li>Questions that work: <i>Is the picture sharp and in focus?</i>, <i>Is there any text or a watermark in the picture?</i>, <i>Is this a photo of food?</i>, <i>Is the main subject looking at the camera?</i></li><li>To keep the NO pictures instead, simply swap the two Save nodes' folders, or type <b>no</b> in Text Match.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Good to know</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>The AI can be wrong on borderline pictures. Check the folders after a big Run.</li><li>Your original pictures are not moved: each one is saved as a copy into its folder.</li><li>Text Match works with any text, not only yes and no: it can look for several words and tells you which one it found.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-ai-prompt-local\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">What AI Prompt needs</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
