      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"model-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Models to download</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Orange. Each one needs a file from the <b>Download Models</b> note.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load CLIP (Qwen3-VL 8B, looks at the pictures)</b> - Qwen3-VL 8B, a language model that can SEE. It looks at each picture and answers the question. It runs on your own PC, nothing is sent online.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your pictures)</b> - Point it at the folder you want to sort and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through, one after the other.</li><li><b>AI Prompt Pixaroma (2. the yes or no question)</b> - Shows each picture to Qwen3-VL with the yes or no question in its formula (the gear). Keep the question SIMPLE, and keep the last part: Answer with one word only: yes or no.</li><li><b>Text Match Pixaroma (3. the answer that keeps a picture)</b> - Checks each answer for the word <b>yes</b> (mode <b>is exactly one of them</b>, so Yes. and YES count too). The picture goes in on <b>value</b> and comes out of <b>if_match</b> only on a yes, out of <b>if_no_match</b> only on a no.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (the pictures the AI said YES to)</b> - Saves the pictures the AI said yes to into <code>ComfyUI/output/With a Person</code>, with their own names.</li><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (the pictures the AI said NO to)</b> - Saves the others into <code>ComfyUI/output/Without a Person</code>. Delete this node if you only want to KEEP the yes pictures.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"model-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Models to download</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Orange. Each one needs a file from the <b>Download Models</b> note.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load CLIP (Qwen3-VL 8B, looks at the pictures)</b> - Qwen3-VL 8B, a language model that can SEE. It looks at each picture and answers the question. It runs on your own PC, nothing is sent online.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your pictures)</b> - Point it at the folder you want to sort and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through, one after the other.</li><li><b>AI Prompt Pixaroma (2. the yes or no question)</b> - Shows each picture to Qwen3-VL with the yes or no question in its formula (the gear). Keep the question SIMPLE, and keep the last part: Answer with one word only: yes or no.</li><li><b>Text Match Pixaroma (3. the answer that keeps a picture)</b> - Checks each answer for the word <b>yes</b> (mode <b>is exactly one of them</b>, so Yes. and YES count too). The picture goes in on <b>value</b> and comes out of <b>if_match</b> only on a yes, out of <b>if_no_match</b> only on a no.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (the pictures the AI said YES to)</b> - Saves the pictures the AI said yes to into <code>ComfyUI/output/With a Person</code>, with their own names.</li><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (the pictures the AI said NO to)</b> - Saves the others into <code>ComfyUI/output/Without a Person</code>. Delete this node if you only want to KEEP the yes pictures.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
